: "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BLOK3", "streams": 3232721, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Motive", "streams": 1045286, "best_position": 10}, {"artist": "Murda", "streams": 618614, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "Ati242", "streams": 491172, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "Ezhel", "streams": 456622, "best_position": 15}, {"artist": "Lvbel C5", "streams": 111470, "best_position": 87}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Lvbel C5", "streams": 111470, "best_position": 87}, {"artist": "Aura", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Ezhel", "streams": 456622, "best_position": 15}, {"artist": "Candan Er\u00e7etin", "streams": 448590, "best_position": 7}, {"artist": "Mabel Matiz", "streams": 291885, "best_position": 37}, {"artist": "Hadise", "streams": 241404, "best_position": 17}, {"artist": "Beng\u00fc", "streams": 169665, "best_position": 32}, {"artist": "G\u00f6ksel", "streams": 157993, "best_position": 42}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": 143765, "best_position": 51}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ajda Pekkan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Uzi", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Hadise", "streams": 241404, "best_position": 17}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Crush", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "rock": {"genre": "rock", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "Rock music is a form of popular music with a prominent vocal melody, accompanied by guitar, drums, and bass. Many styles of rock music also use keyboard instruments such as organ, piano, mellotron, and synthesizers. Other instruments sometimes utilized in rock include saxophone, harmonica, violin, flute, French horn, banjo, melodica, and timpani. Also, less common stringed instruments such as mandolin and sitar are used. Rock music usually has a strong back beat.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Pinhani", "streams": 159713, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": 143765, "best_position": 51}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dolu Kadehi Ters Tut", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Duman", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Hayko Cepkin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "soul": {"genre": "soul", "country_code": "tr", "country_name": "T\u00fcrkiye", "summary": "Soul music is a music genre that combines rhythm and blues and gospel music, originating in the United States.  According to the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, soul is \"music that arose out of the black experience in America through the transmutation of gospel and rhythm & blues into a form of funky, secular testifying.\" The genre occasionally uses improvisational additions, twirls and auxiliary sounds. Catchy rhythms, stressed by handclaps and plastic body moves, are an important feature."